turnkey-version (1.1.3+keel3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Build-Depends no longer names turnkey-netinfo: nothing imports it at
    build time (sysversion imports os, re and subprocess), and a build
    container has no Keel archive to install it from. The runtime
    dependency stays.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 18:30:39 +0000

turnkey-version (1.1.3+keel2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Build-Depends: python3-setuptools, the build backend pyproject.toml
    names (setuptools.build_meta); on a bare trixie the wheel build fails
    without it.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 18:05:15 +0000

turnkey-version (1.1.3+keel1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Build for Keel Linux, Debian 13.
  * The version string comes from /etc/keel_version, with /etc/turnkey_version
    as the fallback: sysversion.get_turnkey_version reads the Keel file first
    whenever the TurnKey path is asked for, which is what the turnkey-version
    command and turnkey-sysinfo do, so neither changes. The keel- prefix is
    accepted beside turnkey- when the string is parsed. One file,
    sysversion/__init__.py; the "TurnKey GNU/Linux" wording of the summary
    line is untouched.

 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 17:42:06 +0000
